0015:     Input structure
0016:     A square grid has one background color and one foreground color. Its side
0017:     length is n*n+n-1, partitioning it into an n by n array of n by n tiles
0018:     separated by single background rows and columns. Some tiles are already
0019:     present; each present tile is filled with foreground except for one
0020:     background pixel at the local coordinate matching the tile's array position.
0021: 
0022:     Rule
0023:     Keep the separator rows and columns background. For every tile position
0024:     (tile row, tile column), fill that n by n tile with the foreground color and
0025:     leave only the local pixel at (tile row, tile column) as background.
0026: 
0027:     Key insight
0028:     The hole inside each tile is a coordinate label for that tile's position in
0029:     the larger tile array, so the sparse input samples define the complete
0030:     position-coded pattern.
